From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Let the cover turn upside down

The cover is a landscape display, so its rotation 180 is the hinge-down,
cameras-up pose. Samsung only lets the rotation sensor pick 180 on tablets
(FW_ALLOW_ALL_ROTATION follows IS_TABLET_DEVICE), so auto-rotate never got
there and users needed a rotation app. Allow every rotation. This also lets
the rotate button offer 180 and keeps 180 when rotation gets locked.

diff --git a/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali b/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
--- a/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
+++ b/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
@@ -3343,7 +3343,8 @@

     sput-boolean v1, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_DEVELOPMENT_DISABLE_STARTING_WINDOW:Z

-    sget-boolean v1, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->IS_TABLET_DEVICE:Z
+    # Onigiri: rotation 180 is the cover's hinge-down pose; let auto-rotate reach it.
+    const/4 v1, 0x1

     sput-boolean v1, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_ALLOW_ALL_ROTATION:Z

